# Automatic commit and push

**Default every session:** work on branch `dev-courtney` (create/checkout from `main` if missing). Publish there automatically—do not wait for the user to ask.

**Remote:** `origin` → https://github.com/AIChief-Courtney/cardscanner.git

## Mandatory end-of-task flow

Whenever this turn changes tracked project files (code, config, Prisma schema/migrations, docs, `.cursor/rules`), before you finish:

1. `git status` and review `git diff` (staged and unstaged).
2. Commit on `dev-courtney` in one or more focused commits (conventional `feat` / `fix` / `chore` / `docs` / `refactor`, imperative subject, short body explaining why).
3. `git push -u origin dev-courtney` on first use, then `git push origin dev-courtney` (or `git push` when upstream is set).
4. Tell the user the commit subject(s) and that `dev-courtney` is pushed.

Skip commits only when: no files changed, or the user explicitly says not to commit/push in that same message.

## Branch policy

- Day-to-day agent edits → `dev-courtney` only (auto commit + auto push).
- `main` → merge or push only when the user explicitly requests it; never force-push `main`.

If you are on `main` after edits, move commits to `dev-courtney` (cherry-pick or new branch) rather than pushing straight to `main` unless the user asked for `main`.

## Never commit

- `.env`, secrets, credentials
- `node_modules/`, `.next/`, `*.log`, build caches (`*.tsbuildinfo`)

## On push failure

Report the error. For non-fast-forward on `dev-courtney`, `git pull --rebase origin dev-courtney` then push again when safe without overwriting others’ work.

This rule overrides generic “commit only when asked” guidance for this repository.